WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.990
Ana has a secret for Ben, a stranger
on the other side of the internet.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.450
They've never met.

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.090
She can scramble it with a key,
turning plaintext into ciphertext.

4
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.810
But Ben needs a key to unscramble it.

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.890
Anything sent along the
cable can be intercepted.

6
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.190
If Ana sends a key, an eavesdropper
could copy it on the way.

7
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:25.150
So how can the message be locked
without ever sending the key?

8
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.610
In this mission, you'll see how encryption
makes intercepted data meaningless

9
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.830
to anyone without the right key.

10
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.850
You'll find out why sharing one key is
the big weakness of symmetric encryption.

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: work out how to lock a
message for someone you have never met.
